                comment: `I first read this at 18 and while Lawrence has become unfashionable in recent years it remains as powerful today as it was to me then - three generations of the Brangwen family, living on the border of Nottinghamshire and Derbyshire, between 1840 and 1905: it was a clear departure from his previous "19th-century" novel Sons and Lovers. Daring, provocative, sexual,  questioning, psychological - a great modernist work. Published in 1915, it was suppressed on the grounds of obscenity, with copies destroyed. Lawrence's importance as a working-class northern writer who broke all taboos cannot be underestimated.`,
