                comment: "Channeling, among other influences, H G Wells, and living under in a totalitarian dictaroship, Bulgakov proved that genre is a meaningless construct with this extraordinary religious, historical, satirical, magical realist work that expands your sense of the things that a novel is capable of.",
                rank: 66,
